{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e","id":102367,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Power Level in 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-30T21:27:09-07:00","id":102367,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Power Level in 3e","content":"I was reading on another thread about how with the Exigents coming in that many of these new Exalts will be able to rival the Solars in power, even when created by Gods, and etc.<br /> <br /> I find that kinda baffling and it led me to question a few things.<br /> <br /> <b>a)</b> Are the Dragon-Blooded going to be more powerful now? In the lore aspect of things it would make no sense for the footsoldiers of the First Age to be as powerful as Solars, but I am willing to go with it.<br /> <br /> <b>b)</b> If they are not more powerful, why will there be Exigents created by not-Elemental Dragons that as powerful as Solars?<br /> <br /> <b>c)</b> I might have made this letter a), but... is there ANY truth in that Exigents might be as powerful as Solars in 3e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:38:25-07:00","id":102380,"title":"","content":"I think that Exigents are supposed to vary massively in their power, and maybe the Exigents of the most powerful Gods might approach Solar power levels.<br /> <br /> I don't really see why that means DBs have to be more powerful though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:42:31-07:00","id":102385,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell, Exigent power levels will fluctuate wildly from Exalt to Exalt, depending on how powerful the god they're made from was and how much of themselves they gave up.<br /> <br /> DBs were footsoldiers in the first age for two major reasons and a third that I can't remember right now:<br /> 1) There were more of them than any other Exalt type. This still holds true, since the one bit of fiction we have on Exigents indicates that it is a laborous, difficult process to get approved for an Exigent, and it's possible the god that the Exigent is derived from can die.<br /> <br /> 2) DBs worked best in teams, which makes sense given that their powers are derived from the highest parts of Gaia's titanic being. Exigents are created one at a time, and their powers are all derived from different beings who may very well have as much connection to each other as UCS does to my left foot's toenails. So it's unlikely they would complement each others' powers as well.<br /> <br /> Granted, they were BUILT that way, but you get the idea. And Exigents don't fill either of those niches in the Exalted host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:43:09-07:00","id":102386,"title":"","content":"A. As far as I know, no. I believe they ARE making the difference in power between Terrestrials and Celestials a bit less, but on the whole, Dragon-Bloods are the weakest of the main Exalted host.<br /> <br /> B. It's a matter of how they were made. The Terrestrial Exalted were created weaker so that they could pass along their powers by the blood... I would imagine that, if they were any more powerful, the Exaltation could not be passed on biologically. If they had any reason to, I would think that one of the Elemental Dragons could, theoretically, take an Exigence and create an Exalt more powerful that a Dragon-Blooded, but s/he likely wouldn't be able to make more of the same by breeding.<br /> <br /> C. Yes, but I believe it's only in potential. If you wanted to, you could create an Exigent that is every bit as powerful as a Solar*. However, he would likely be a single instance, his Exaltation probably wouldn't pass on to a new host, and we don't know how Exigents and Exalts might differ (if they do at all, of course). Setting-wise, it probably doesn't happen, if only because it's likely very rare for a god to be able to pass on that much power through the Exigence, even by sacrificing their own life. However, if you, as a player, can think of a good reason why it could happen, then the developers are merely giving you the tools to do so.<br /> <br /> I'll try to answer anything I may have been unclear or wrong about.<br /> <br /> Edit* Likewise, you could make an Exigent weaker than a Dragon-Blood, perhaps even much weaker, who passes on their powers by 'infecting' others blood with blood to blood contact. I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:47:10-07:00","id":102388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e#post102367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>a)</b> Are the Dragon-Blooded going to be more powerful now? In the lore aspect of things it would make no sense for the footsoldiers of the First Age to be as powerful as Solars, but I am willing to go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is somewhat tricky, given the somewhat nebulous definition of power. I think the current goal is for their to be less of a gap between 3ed Dragonblooded and Solars than their was between 2ed Dragonblooded and Solars, especially when it comes to combat. I don't think they're going to match Solars one on one, but I think you won't need quite the swarm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e#post102367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>b)</b> If they are not more powerful, why will there be Exigents created by not-Elemental Dragons that as powerful as Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because their are still fewer Exigents than Dragonblooded and the powerful ones presumably do not have any way to pass on their power like Dragonblooded. Adding a few more people who can possibly match a Solar does not equal adding 20000+ beings who can.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e#post102367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>c)</b> I might have made this letter a), but... is there ANY truth in that Exigents might be as powerful as Solars in 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, though a bit incomplete. I don't recall any blanket statement that Exigents are going to be as powerful as Solars across the board, just that within a particular area they can reach that power. The issue for them is largely that what area depends on the Exigent, and that such a level of power is not a constant. For example, Strawmaiden Janest was stated, I believe, to be about equal in combat to a Solar...assuming she was on the fields what were from the god who empowered her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:24:03-07:00","id":102397,"title":"","content":"As to passing on their power, I'd assume that Exigents don't pass on their power at all by any method. They're a one-off thing made by a God. A core part of what being an Exigent is about is supposed to be &quot;a god gave up some of his/her power to create you&quot;, not &quot;you inherited your power from your father/previous incarnation&quot;.<br /> I could be wrong, but that's what I'd expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:39:19-07:00","id":102410,"title":"","content":"Thanks, folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:42:27-07:00","id":102411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102397#post102397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to passing on their power, I'd assume that Exigents don't pass on their power at all by any method. They're a one-off thing made by a God. A core part of what being an Exigent is about is supposed to be &quot;a god gave up some of his/her power to create you&quot;, not &quot;you inherited your power from your father/previous incarnation&quot;.<br /> I could be wrong, but that's what I'd expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to that appears to be the same answer regarding virtually every other facet of Exigents: &quot;It depends on the Exigent.&quot; There was a quote on heritability that's bothering me, because I'm <i>sure</i> I saw it on the EX3 Wiki, but it seems to have mysteriously vanished at some point. :/ It hailed from the old forums, too, so full context is lost. Still, courtesy of Nishkriya, <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/3181\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> was Holden's response to a poster's list of various ways in which an Exigent might pass on its power:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup.<br /> <br /> (The majority of Exigents throughout history have been the last kind-- although, note, that's not always power-related. There have been some hellaciously powerful one-and-done Exigents.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The last kind&quot; indeed referred to one-shot Exigents that didn't/couldn't pass on their power at all. I don't remember the other items on the list, but there were some inventive ones, in addition to the typical Celestial style and (I believe) passing it on to one's descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:44:36-07:00","id":102415,"title":"","content":"Some Exigents can pass on their power, and they can pass their powers on in a wide range of ways.<br /> <br /> You could have an Exigent who passes on their power to whomever beats them in a foot race. Or passes on their power to their seventh son. Or when that Exigent dies, a tree grows over their grave and produces a single, golden pear after 100 years, and whoever eats it gains their power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102386#post102386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Terrestrial Exalted were created weaker so that they could pass along their powers by the blood...</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Elemental Dragons gave their power to make some Exalted who could breed more Exalted and the power level ended up where it did. I don't think they said to themselves 'we can't add any more power, Captain, or the dilithium matrix will blow!'<br /> <br /> Solars are the only sort of Exalted that Sol could have produced. Lunars are the only sort of Exalted that Luna could have produced. Terrestrials are the only sort of Exalted the dragons could have produced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-31-2014, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T22:45:19-07:00","id":102416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102397#post102397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to passing on their power, I'd assume that Exigents don't pass on their power at all by any method. They're a one-off thing made by a God. A core part of what being an Exigent is about is supposed to be &quot;a god gave up some of his/her power to create you&quot;, not &quot;you inherited your power from your father/previous incarnation&quot;.<br /> I could be wrong, but that's what I'd expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have said that some Exigents _can_ pass on their power, whether like a DB, a Celestial, or by their own personalised method. That's kinda the idea of the Exigents - everything about their Exaltation and powers is personalised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 03-31-2014, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:02:00-07:00","id":102420,"title":"","content":"Exigents aren't a specific class of being, so much as an umbrella to keep all the 'Sun gives power so a God can craft his own Exaltation', so they can be pretty much anything. Some of them will be as strong as a Solar, but then again, I expect those to be vanishingly rare, and for us to pretty much not see any canonical examples of that, left only as an option to STs and players. There are already several Hekatonkire, Gods, Third Circles and Crazy Unique Oddities that rival Solars in some way or another, and I expect the same would be true for the Exigents; they will probably still lack some of the Solar tools, and all of their niche, too. So it's not a threat to the Solar's niche, just one of those odd rare things that can stand up to them, no stranger than bumping into Five Days Darkness along the way.<br /> <br /> And as for DBs... devs play favorites, and Exigents are their new hotness. DBs won't be changed because of them, but will still be fine as what they used to be. Like most of the 'old Exalts', apart from maybe Solars (and certainly Sidereals), they shouldn't be expected to shine (Lunars and Abyssals will certainly suffer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 03-31-2014, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:29:36-07:00","id":102438,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'd expect that the DBs will get a new breath of life with their new book. I imagine they'll be more thematically firm, work better, etc, while still being bottom of the pile, power-wise.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are going in a slightly new direction, away from the &quot;mirror Solars&quot;, so that'll make them a bit more interesting, while I can well see Lunars having a lot of work done to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:43:22-07:00","id":102447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102438#post102438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'd expect that the DBs will get a new breath of life with their new book. I imagine they'll be more thematically firm, work better, etc, while still being bottom of the pile, power-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh, so do I! I have good hopes for What Fire Has Wrought. As I just said, I expect them to be fine! The question of the thread is basically if they will get something new, if this new splat is getting so much, and I was answering no, as the current team never tried to keep all coolness equal, to preserve old Exalts or make up for lost niches. Not all Exalted are created equal to everyone, unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:48:38-07:00","id":102452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102447#post102447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bOh, so do I! I have good hopes for What Fire Has Wrought. As I just said, I expect them to be fine! The question of the thread is basically if they will get something new, if this new splat is getting so much, and I was answering no, as the current team never tried to keep all coolness equal, to preserve old Exalts or make up for lost niches. Not all Exalted are created equal to everyone, unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and this is why I stay away from Exalted as much as I can =(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:50:04-07:00","id":102455,"title":"","content":"DB's stay around and are useful no matter what because of their synergy and numbers. I don't even think the God of Sentai could make better Power Rangers than a Sworn Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> Exigents vary wildly in scope and power, but there's no God in Creation that has enough in it to make as many Exigents with a proper average competency as there are Dragon Blooded. You can't rely on there being 10,000 Chosen of the Harvest to back you up in a war. I think it might have been mentioned somewhere that even the most powerful Gods that petition for Exigents can only make a few hand-fulls, if that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:52:51-07:00","id":102460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102420#post102420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as for DBs... devs play favorites, and Exigents are their new hotness. DBs won't be changed because of them, but will still be fine as what they used to be. Like most of the 'old Exalts', apart from maybe Solars (and certainly Sidereals), they shouldn't be expected to shine (Lunars and Abyssals will certainly suffer.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of the new Exalt types is to help the old ones shine.<br /> Also I think the only way Abyssals could suffer <b>worse</b> than they did in 2nd edition would be if their supplement got replaced by a two page spread explaining how to convert a Solar character into an Abyssal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:07:30-07:00","id":102466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102452#post102452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, and this is why I stay away from Exalted as much as I can =(</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't! The current design team is human, and plays favorites, yeah... but they are also VERY good at what they do, and I'm sure it will be full of fun things for you to add to your Dragon-Blooded games. Just houserule more coolness to them there, Exalted has always been the Homebrew Game, after all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102460#post102460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of the new Exalt types is to help the old ones shine.</div> </div> </div> </div>How well remains to be seen, of course; their track record on that isn't good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102460#post102460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I think the only way Abyssals could suffer <b>worse</b> than they did in 2nd edition would be if their supplement got replaced by a two page spread explaining how to convert a Solar character into an Abyssal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preeeeetty much!<br /> <br /> Mind, you're talking to someone who looked at 2e, went 'what the {expletive} is this {expletive}', put it down and walked on, so what they are in 2e didn't enter that; I still remember when Abyssals were one of the most popular types in 1e (and they still had a metric ton of flaws then.)<br /> <br /> I expect the current design team to do a better job with... all splats than 2e did, and even than 1e did (excepting Sidereals, maybe); when the dust settles, though, I also expect humanity to show through and for favoritism to be clear in design decisions as it has been in the quotes we've seen. I am speaking specifically on how each Exalted type will stack in terms of coolness against EACH OTHER in 3e (as the thread was pointing to), and not how they will compare to their earlier counterparts. Which will be favorably, I'm sure. Lunars 1e was a trainwreck, 2e was bland, Abyssals 2e was a wretch; Holden and co. could probably do better than that in their sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 03-31-2014, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:37:41-07:00","id":102478,"title":"","content":"A.) The Dragon-Blooded will be less poorly written mechanically. Meaning the power they're ascribed in the narrative will come closer to matching the power they actually have in play, but that narrative position won't change much.<br /> <br /> B.) I don't fully understand what you're asking, but I'll take a shot. First,there's no confirmation yet that <i>Elementals</i> even can make Exigents. It's been spoken of as something belonging to <i>Gods</i> alone. I'm not sure what degree of distinction between those two things that 3E will continue to recognize, but it's pretty distinct right now. <i>If</i> Elementals can make Exigents, their Exigents will not be &quot;Dragon-Blooded, but more powerful,&quot; because no individual Elemental represents their Element as fully and broadly as the Five Elemental Dragons. They all attach their own unique spin to the concept. An Exigent is never &quot;Chosen of [Concept]&quot;, they are &quot;Chosen of [<i>God</i> of Concept]&quot;, and that's a huge difference. So even if the Gardullis is permitted to commission Chosen, they will be substantially different from the Fire Aspect Dragon-Blooded, because the flame of the Gardullis is far more limited conceptually than the flame of Hesiesh.<br /> <br /> C.) Holden has said that Dragon Blooded typically define the bottom floor of Exalted power, much like Solars define its ceiling, and that individual Exigents may fall anywhere on that spectrum, depending who empowered them, and what specific competency is being measured. Some of the Exigents may be constructed in such a way that they Reincarnate like Celestials, or Breed True like Terrestrials, or maybe even something wholly unique to that Exigent type, but such a system would be one of many demands on the limited power being applied to creating them, and Holden says <i>most</i> Exigents are one-shots. The God empowers their Chosen, and when that Chosen dies, that's the end of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:49:16-07:00","id":102482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102466#post102466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How well remains to be seen, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the main way Exigents help Dragon-Blooded is that they're an Exalt type that's not considered Anathema (Anathema specifically means &quot;those bastards we overthrew&quot; not &quot;it's not like us! KILL IT!&quot;).<br /> It significantly expands the options for who Dynastic Dragon-Blooded can work with (though maybe with a little unease) and not be betraying their entire culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:59:04-07:00","id":102488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102482#post102482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the main way Exigents help Dragon-Blooded is that they're an Exalt type that's not considered Anathema (Anathema specifically means &quot;those bastards we overthrew&quot; not &quot;it's not like us! KILL IT!&quot;).<br /> It significantly expands the options for who Dynastic Dragon-Blooded can work with (though maybe with a little unease) and not be betraying their entire culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? This I like!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T01:33:58-07:00","id":102494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102482#post102482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the main way Exigents help Dragon-Blooded is that they're an Exalt type that's not considered Anathema (Anathema specifically means &quot;those bastards we overthrew&quot; not &quot;it's not like us! KILL IT!&quot;).<br /> It significantly expands the options for who Dynastic Dragon-Blooded can work with (though maybe with a little unease) and not be betraying their entire culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that hardcore Immaculates will not be keen on Exigents (it's clear evidence that a god and a human have been working together, very naughty) but that more practical Dragonblooded will be okay with working with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T02:35:18-07:00","id":102510,"title":"","content":"The Exigence itself can allow gods to fashion Exalted of greater power than their own nature would imply.<br /> <br /> This is probably not an exploitable, mechanistic thing. I'd say it might depend somewhat on the depth of the spirit's need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:08:24-07:00","id":102524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e#post102367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading on another thread about how with the Exigents coming in that many of these new Exalts will be able to rival the Solars in power, even when created by Gods, and etc.<br /> <br /> I find that kinda baffling and it led me to question a few things.<br /> <br /> <b>a)</b> Are the Dragon-Blooded going to be more powerful now? In the lore aspect of things it would make no sense for the footsoldiers of the First Age to be as powerful as Solars, but I am willing to go with it.<br /> <br /> <b>b)</b> If they are not more powerful, why will there be Exigents created by not-Elemental Dragons that as powerful as Solars?<br /> <br /> <b>c)</b> I might have made this letter a), but... is there ANY truth in that Exigents might be as powerful as Solars in 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An Exigent isn't one kind of Exalt. They vary from being less powerful than Terrestrial, to rivaling Solar Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:15:33-07:00","id":102527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102466#post102466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How well remains to be seen, of course; their track record on that isn't good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which track record? The one where every book my name has been on has gone platinum, or the one where I worked on the most-funded tabletop Kickstarter in the world? *mic drop*<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:37:49-07:00","id":102534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102527#post102527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which track record? The one where every book my name has been on has gone platinum, or the one where I worked on the most-funded tabletop Kickstarter in the world? *mic drop*<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Contextually, the most likely thing Colapso was talking about is your track record of introducing new splats, or using new splats to make older ones seem cooler. Which is quite confusing, seeing as you haven't published any new splats yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T04:54:42-07:00","id":102552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102534#post102534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contextually, the most likely thing Colapso was talking about is your track record of introducing new splats, or using new splats to make older ones seem cooler. Which is quite confusing, seeing as you haven't published any new splats yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some people does think Infernal is the unholy lovechild of the current writer if my memory from all those old Ink Monkey thread is correct~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T05:23:20-07:00","id":102564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102552#post102552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, some people does think Infernal is the unholy lovechild of the current writer if my memory from all those old Ink Monkey thread is correct~</div> </div> </div> </div>But Holden was only a playtester for Infernals, and John was not involved with the game at all until half a year later!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T06:04:18-07:00","id":102582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102564#post102564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Holden was only a playtester for Infernals, and John was not involved with the game at all until half a year later!</div> </div> </div> </div>And Eric did the Helltech chapter, iirc. Which generally gets overshadowed by the highs and lows of the chapters before it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T06:19:10-07:00","id":102586,"title":"","content":"The Helltech or Infernal Wonders or whatever that chapter is called is something I view as rather a flawed gem, something that made a lot more sense when I learned that Eric got that job after the writer originally assigned to it quit and took all the work with them, and Eric had to have it ready to roll out in a matter of weeks.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_lpbay4tAoL1qk2t5co1_r1_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:03:21-07:00","id":102624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102482#post102482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the main way Exigents help Dragon-Blooded is that they're an Exalt type that's not considered Anathema (Anathema specifically means &quot;those bastards we overthrew&quot; not &quot;it's not like us! KILL IT!&quot;).<br /> It significantly expands the options for who Dynastic Dragon-Blooded can work with (though maybe with a little unease) and not be betraying their entire culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can very well be a bad thing. Exigents are the homebrew Exalted, and nobody ever made something Terrestrial-level if they could avoid it; there were always few TMAs, few Terrestrial Circle Spells, and I'm one of the handful of people I've ever seen introduce new Terrestrial Exalted, rather than trying to make everything Celestial. Exigents were suggested as part of a Wyld Hunt's makeup, so they will be NPC and PC material... and will probably end up outshining DBs in their own games, being more powerful NPCs and PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102527#post102527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which track record? The one where every book my name has been on has gone platinum, or the one where I worked on the most-funded tabletop Kickstarter in the world? *mic drop*<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>John, in the very same post you quoted I went on to say that I do expect you to be successful. And I do expect you to do a great job. So that is in no way a reply. The track record mention is only in niche protection. If I'm not mistaken, Holden's the writer of Transcendent Howl of the Devil-Tiger. By the time I came back to looking at the forums - because of my friends gushing about YOUR WORK - there were several threads where people talked about how Infernals were better Solars than Solars, and certainly better Lunars than Lunars, and trying to find what the Solar or Lunar 'thing' even is. I expect you will make terrific work overall, but I do not expect Dragon-Blooded, Lunars and Abyssals to shine as bright as Infernals, Liminals, Alchemicals and Sidereals (one of Holden's favorites) once you're done.<br /> <br /> I'd love to be proven wrong.<br /> <br /> (I thought Holden's involvement predated the Broken-Winged Crane, though; that does alleviate some worries. The helltech chapter is another one of those 'well, this is awesome, but also gives them cooler toys than everyone for the sake of giving them cooler toys'. See also: I expect their job to be excellent, I expect it to play favorites.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:19:02-07:00","id":102632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102624#post102624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nobody ever made something Terrestrial-level if they could avoid it</div> </div> </div> </div>How certain are you of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:27:40-07:00","id":102637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102632#post102632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How certain are you of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vanishingly small number of Terrestrial Martial Arts, the fact that basically all fan-proposed splats are Celestial in level? I'd love it if people DID make more Terrestrial-level things, but going by old and new wiki, the Terrestrial crunch-love is a rare beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:33:44-07:00","id":102643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102624#post102624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not expect Dragon-Blooded, Lunars and Abyssals to shine as bright as Infernals, Liminals, Alchemicals and Sidereals (one of Holden's favorites) once you're done.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez, if you'd only seen the amount of discussion time that Holden and John have put into Lunars and Abyssals respectively...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:39:29-07:00","id":102647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102637#post102637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vanishingly small number of Terrestrial Martial Arts, the fact that basically all fan-proposed splats are Celestial in level? I'd love it if people DID make more Terrestrial-level things, but going by old and new wiki, the Terrestrial crunch-love is a rare beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vanishingly small?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts\" target=\"_blank\"> http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> I dunno man, I'm pretty sure you're seeing what you're determined to see on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:46:15-07:00","id":102654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102647#post102647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vanishingly small?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts\" target=\"_blank\"> http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TerrestrialMartialArts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I dunno man, I'm pretty sure you're seeing what you're determined to see on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? In comparison with the Celestial arts? You can fit all TMAs inside on of the CMA sections.<br /> <br /> Plus, a few of those are either mine or by people who played with me, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:58:12-07:00","id":102666,"title":"","content":"I'd say that's probably because in second edition the terrestrial mechanics sucked. I mean, for starters, when one of the most important things to ensure one's survival in combat is perfect defenses, something which is one of the notable things Terrestrials lack? That's not going to make people want to make Terrestrials. Hell, one of the only things that made people assign Alchemicals to the Celestial level is the fact that they had perfects. The fact that Dragonblooded also had some decent problems mechanically in other areas didn't help matters. <br /> <br /> Also, there's the problem that, since most games seemed to be Celestial or Solar level in 2nd, well, you end up with the most homebrew for the things you really use(plus I don't think most people really homebrew stuff that's going to be NPC only). This hurt TMA for predictable reasons: martial arts generally were assumed to at best be about equal with charms of the Exalted of their teir, so at best a Celestial taking TMA is spending xp on weaker charms, and the charms still cost the same amount.<br /> <br /> It looks like several things are going to be changing for 3rd, though. For instance, the elimination of the CMA/TMA divide, and the hopefully more robust Dragonblooded charms.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:18:24-07:00","id":102684,"title":"","content":"In 2e, the celestial power level design paradigm could be roughly boiled down to &quot;effortlessly ignores everything weaker&quot;, which wasn't very inviting to terrestrial-level guys. Judging by the Solar Charms spoiled so far for 3e, the new design paradigm is more in the vein of &quot;celestial stuff has an advantage&quot;, which is workable from a lower power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:21:53-07:00","id":102691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102632#post102632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How certain are you of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may not be very prolific, but of the things I have made, most of them have been Terrestrial Charms or TMAs. I find the expected power level of a Solar Charm to make it lack direction. Restriction makes it easier to draw on appropriate themes and simultaneously keep an appropriate power level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:26:36-07:00","id":102697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102643#post102643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez, if you'd only seen the amount of discussion time that Holden and John have put into Lunars and Abyssals respectively...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Someone who hasn't is going to have a very different underlying impression about where those splats are going. Luckily, Marin on the EX3 What We Know Wiki has collected rather a lot of what they've had to say on <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Dragon-Blooded\" target=\"_blank\">the Dragon-Blooded</a>, <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Abyssals\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a>, and <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Lunars</a>, along with the other Exalted and a bunch of other stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:30:54-07:00","id":102703,"title":"","content":"The whole deal where the only way to find out who actually wrote what and under what direction is to gather secret trinkets of wisdom from the forums like a magpie makes it very confusing to form opinions of writers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:37:45-07:00","id":102710,"title":"","content":"Oh, no, it makes it easy to <i>form </i>opinions of writers. It's just that on average they're going to tend towards &quot;writers are dicks&quot;, because the proof otherwise is all sorts of hidden :P<br /> <br /> (Seriously, the common opinion among my group, which only follows Exalted tangentially, is that Vance is the only person in the current team they wouldn't consider bad)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:54:22-07:00","id":102727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102624#post102624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That can very well be a bad thing. Exigents are the homebrew Exalted, and nobody ever made something Terrestrial-level if they could avoid it; there were always few TMAs, few Terrestrial Circle Spells, and I'm one of the handful of people I've ever seen introduce new Terrestrial Exalted, rather than trying to make everything Celestial. Exigents were suggested as part of a Wyld Hunt's makeup, so they will be NPC and PC material... and will probably end up outshining DBs in their own games, being more powerful NPCs and PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone with no qualms about making the game revolve around their special snowflake character can ruin everyone's fun.<br /> <br /> Situation normal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:02:18-07:00","id":102738,"title":"","content":"I always thought that there're more Terrestrial spells than Celestial/Solar Circle, at least that what I remembered from the old Exalted wiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:29:13-07:00","id":102759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102637#post102637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vanishingly small number of Terrestrial Martial Arts, the fact that basically all fan-proposed splats are Celestial in level? I'd love it if people DID make more Terrestrial-level things, but going by old and new wiki, the Terrestrial crunch-love is a rare beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>People tend to love power, and I agree with you. The Terrestrial material is very rare, and it shows on polls where people can ask for new stuff. It is never Terrestrial. I barely get ANY comissions involving the Terrestrial Exalted. In fact, only one person has ever asked me for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:41:12-07:00","id":102772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102624#post102624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I thought Holden's involvement predated <b>the Broken-Winged Crane</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe he wrote the Alchemical Charms, but I forget if that came out before or after <b>the Broken-Winged Crane</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:50:11-07:00","id":102780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102624#post102624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents were suggested as part of a Wyld Hunt's makeup, so they will be NPC and PC material... and will probably end up outshining DBs in their own games, being more powerful NPCs and PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Exigents as part of a Wyld Hunt&quot; isn't something I've heard before. Where did that come up? In addition to Lioness's observation above, it doesn't seem any more likely that Exigents will be a part of a Wyld Hunt than, say a god-blooded. Part of it stems from relative scarcity,* part of it stems from Exigents not having remotely the same incentive to sign up with a Hunt as a Terrestrial, and part of it stems from how Immaculate dogma plainly isn't very big on them (for all it doesn't inherently regard them as Anathema) :<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents basically fall under the same heading as God-Blooded-- the result of improper congress between gods and mortals, and thus shameful and karmically banjaxed, but not the end of the world or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside how there's no guarantee an Exigent will be potent enough to outshine the Wyld Hunt Dragonblooded in the Terrestrials' areas of expertise, an Exigent on a Wyld Hunt feels like a sizeable exception to the norm.<br /> <br /> * Exigents have been largely gone for about as long as Solars have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:16:56-07:00","id":102795,"title":"","content":"I actually specifically hope that DBs are not more powerful. They're interesting because they aren't powerful, particularly in areas outside combat. They're not the legendary warrior-kings of the world, they're footsoldiers. Solar exalted are not about what can you do but what will you do, dragonblooded are absolutely about what can you do. A dawn slaying a behemoth is not really a challenge usually, even without the rest of his circle he can slay a giant monster, possibly in a single sword stroke. A DB can't do that, he needs his whole circle to work together, a plan, lots of resources and a bunch of luck. They're two different stories, making DBs more powerful stops you from telling an interesting story about how will you ever defeat the behemoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:48:55-07:00","id":102818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102710#post102710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Seriously, the common opinion among my group, which only follows Exalted tangentially, is that Vance is the only person in the current team they wouldn't consider bad)</div> </div> </div> </div>;________;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:49:05-07:00","id":102819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102795#post102795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually specifically hope that DBs are not more powerful. They're interesting because they aren't powerful, particularly in areas outside combat. They're not the legendary warrior-kings of the world, they're footsoldiers. Solar exalted are not about what can you do but what will you do, dragonblooded are absolutely about what can you do. A dawn slaying a behemoth is not really a challenge usually, even without the rest of his circle he can slay a giant monster, possibly in a single sword stroke. A DB can't do that, he needs his whole circle to work together, a plan, lots of resources and a bunch of luck. They're two different stories, making DBs more powerful stops you from telling an interesting story about how will you ever defeat the behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they could get buffed a bit without obviating that story arc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:05:16-07:00","id":102832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102795#post102795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A dawn slaying a behemoth is not really a challenge usually, even without the rest of his circle he can slay a giant monster, possibly in a single sword stroke.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the worst aspects of 2e Solars right here. &quot;Here's a potentially interesting conflict posed by a unique monst... *sigh* ah well, moving on.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:15:01-07:00","id":102840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102832#post102832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the worst aspects of 2e Solars right here. &quot;Here's a potentially interesting conflict posed by a unique monst... *sigh* ah well, moving on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2e was pretty bad about this, due to damage inflation and the proliferation of badtouch that followed in the wake of keyword defenses, but even back in 1e it could be kind of silly. One GM ran a game where we had to fight a bunch of unique giant monsters in various places in order to secure specific locations, and each one was built as a set-piece battle with a specialized gimmick for beating the boss, and I think for at least half of them we just steamrolled over the gimmick and beat the monster through brute force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:18:46-07:00","id":102842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102795#post102795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Solar exalted are not about what can you do but what will you do, dragonblooded are absolutely about what can you do. A dawn slaying a behemoth is not really a challenge usually, even without the rest of his circle he can slay a giant monster, possibly in a single sword stroke.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a splat that's not supposed to be about what you <i>can</i> do, they sure get an awful lot of wordcount delineating exactly what they can do. A bit inefficient of them to write up a ten-step attack resolution system with complicated second-by-second timing rules when they could have just written &quot;Dawn wins effortlessly,&quot; isn't is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:31:38-07:00","id":102852,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that they're not <i>specifically</i> aiming to change the DB power level (and DBs are still meant to be noticeably weaker than Celestials), but that groups of DBs will probably do better taking on Solars because of a variety of broader changes to the system.<br /> <br /> For instance, we've been told that one major goal of 3e is to make it matter more when you're outnumbered. They've indicated that they're mostly taking out or toning down 'static' defenses (which were a huge part of Solar power in the previous two editions), and obviously perfecting everything isn't supposed to be an option, either. These things tend to help DBs just because the places where 2e mechanics went all pair-shaped tended to be places where the DBs would lose out.<br /> <br /> So DBs will still be at a noticeable disadvantage against an equally combat-experienced Solar, but the system is probably going to be less likely to lead to overwhelmingly one-sided curbstomps like you had in 2e when you fought a Solar who had IAM up or when you started to compare unfooable attacks and perfect defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:43:47-07:00","id":102863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102818#post102818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">;________;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay, Eric, my table likes you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T14:47:56-07:00","id":102946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102863#post102863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's okay, Eric, my table likes you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My chair says it likes you too Eric. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T15:15:38-07:00","id":102964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102842#post102842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a splat that's not supposed to be about what you <i>can</i> do, they sure get an awful lot of wordcount delineating exactly what they can do. A bit inefficient of them to write up a ten-step attack resolution system with complicated second-by-second timing rules when they could have just written &quot;Dawn wins effortlessly,&quot; isn't is?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For a splat that's not supposed to be about what you <i>can</i> do, they sure get an awful lot of wordcount delineating exactly what they can do. A bit inefficient of them to write up a ten-step attack resolution system with complicated second-by-second timing rules when they could have just written &quot;Dawn wins effortlessly,&quot; isn't is?[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> For people who are fighting within the same tier of combat it works out a lot better, Dawn vs Dawn for instance. Outside that it can become kind of pointless though, not instantly but quickly. For example my last session had six essence six DBs and one essence nine DB against a Dawn, and even then they only won through a combination of the Dawn not having a lot of good charms and he didn't use the charms that he had as effectively as he could have.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I like it, but I've been told by a lot of people that this is working as intended to a certain extent. I've never really understood it but they say that Solar stories are more about choosing to do something for moral or personal reasons and how your actions have consequences. Like marching into the Realm deliberative and spinning your sword around to kill all the senators, it seems like a good idea at first since they're backstabbing impotent politicians, but maybe it will destabilize the whole Realm. Also you kill Poramo who's everyone's best friend, seriously just look at that handsome bastard. So yes, while it's totally possible for you to throw up IAM and a few other choice scene long defenses and then MCL into the heart of the Empire, kill everyone there and then leave before the Sidereals finish crapping themselves...do you really want to?<br /> <br /> Again, I don't quite understand this, but it seems to be a somewhat popular opinion. Solar stories about having the power to change the whole world, asking the question &quot;what are you going to change it into?&quot;. Maybe that's just a bullet point on the back of the book that people are taking too seriously though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T16:19:06-07:00","id":102983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102964#post102964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I don't quite understand this, but it seems to be a somewhat popular opinion. Solar stories about having the power to change the whole world, asking the question &quot;what are you going to change it into?&quot;. Maybe that's just a bullet point on the back of the book that people are taking too seriously though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The feeling of empowerment, shooting for the stars, bringing sweeping change to the world around you and living to see the consequences of your choices are very much intended. The fact that the system expresses those themes through boring can't-touch-this effects, not so much.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think your perception of Dragon-Blooded as telling a fundamentally different story is very much distorted by those bad mechanics. A tale of DBs is also supposed to be a tale of empowerment and entitlement, subtly colored by the systems making them not quite as powerful as other Exalted, rather than the story of underdogs always swimming uphill that the system actually paints. I mean, by the very way the setting is written, the Realm is the default Big Bad, an idea that was hard to sell in light of just how much DBs sucked mechanically, and ultimately got forgotten when the system started dwelling more on the high Essence power range and the transcendent beings inhabiting it's upper echelons - but this is an aberration, not the intended outcome! <br /> <br /> In a perfect world, a Solar wouldn't feel like he got the whole world handed on a silver platter without even asking, and a DB would feel like an elemental badass and a worthy heir to the titan-slaying army of ancient myths, all the while retaining a palpable difference in raw power between the two and all the nuances this adds to their respective stories. Hopefully, 3e will make it close enough to the ideal to make both ends of the power spectrum playable and fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T16:44:25-07:00","id":102998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102637#post102637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vanishingly small number of Terrestrial Martial Arts, the fact that basically all fan-proposed splats are Celestial in level? I'd love it if people DID make more Terrestrial-level things, but going by old and new wiki, the Terrestrial crunch-love is a rare beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that 2e handled dragon-blooded very, very badly. The DB are probably my favorite splat lore wise, but were mechanically difficult to play in 2e due to nebulous charm text/mechanics and 2e's lethality issues. This has really limited the number of times that I actually played terrestrials in 2e. Were that situation to change (and I suspect that it might), then I expect that you'll find a lot of the DB fans coming home to roost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T16:52:03-07:00","id":103002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102772#post102772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe he wrote the Alchemical Charms, but I forget if that came out <b>before or after</b> the Broken-Winged Crane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that tends to be one of the big problems surrounding the Broken-Winged Crane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1225-naz","name":"Naz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1225_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T16:59:37-07:00","id":103004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102983#post102983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a perfect world, a Solar wouldn't feel like he got the whole world handed on a silver platter without even asking, and a DB would feel like an elemental badass and a worthy heir to the titan-slaying army of ancient myths, all the while retaining a palpable difference in raw power between the two and all the nuances this adds to their respective stories. Hopefully, 3e will make it close enough to the ideal to make both ends of the power spectrum playable and fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is indeed the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:31:28-07:00","id":103020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102710#post102710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Seriously, the common opinion among my group, which only follows Exalted tangentially, is that Vance is the only person in the current team they wouldn't consider bad)</div> </div> </div> </div>?__________?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:48:10-07:00","id":103026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102998#post102998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the issue is that 2e handled dragon-blooded very, very badly. The DB are probably my favorite splat lore wise, but were mechanically difficult to play in 2e due to nebulous charm text/mechanics and 2e's lethality issues. This has really limited the number of times that I actually played terrestrials in 2e. Were that situation to change (and I suspect that it might), then I expect that you'll find a lot of the DB fans coming home to roost.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the case even in 1e, though. Even when you had DB games coming out left and right, people just wanted to punch out of their power tier in terms of mechanics.<br /> <br /> (And yes, Oramus linked all the TMAs, three by me, four by my best friend, even, but people were putting out INSANE amounts of fan-content back then; that's actually... very, very few in context.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Though, in the topic of not considering bad... I'd like to retract my earlier statements. I had a view of the line which... I do believe is right, but thing is, I talked to Holden, and it is also how he sees it. I was just... pining the wrong things at his feet, at their feet, and I'm sorry. I do have faith the current team will handle the Core Exalted well now.<br /> <br /> (And Tchokes shouldn't stay away from Exalted. We should all do a PBP when DBs 3e comes out or something!)<br /> <br /> (I seem to love parenthesis.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 03-31-2014, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:58:03-07:00","id":103032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102983#post102983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a perfect world, a Solar wouldn't feel like he got the whole world handed on a silver platter without even asking</div> </div> </div> </div>In particular, I feel that it ultimately robs a certain measure of credibility from Solars if we assume that, even if their most meaningful challenges come from the moral implications of what they set out and manage to do, their ultimate peril from making the &quot;wrong&quot; choice is that they'll have to live with their sadfeels. It doesn't really feel true to the setting if Solars are presented as insulated from the possibility that their choices can actually make people mad enough to want to kill them, and that such people can actually succeed.<br /> <br /> That's what I feel when I see anything that objects to different priorities of Solar power on the grounds that Solars should be powerful enough that they get to treat the world as a moral puzzle they have to try and solve.<br /> <br /> It's why I prefer proposed Third Edition Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe to the Second Edition one; the Third Edition one still allows for and implies the possibility that if, say, I use it to try and direct Sova away from cultural hatred of Yugash, that individuals within Sova who, for whatever personal or political reasons (like being a reactionary or having actually been witness to the desecration of the Ixut soulgems) have a direct sense of hatred towards Yugash, might still engage in things to try and redirect Sova, including targeting the actual Solar, recognised as a source of the change and designated an unwelcome interloper.<br /> <br /> To the extent that fighting behemoths might be part of this, well... most of the time, it probably isn't, the behemoth is just a big monster for you to be impressive about fighting (though part of being impressive is having a meaningful possibility of danger). Still, there might be some other practical or moral considerations, whether it's the behemoth being a blight on certain people and facing meaningful peril for their sake, or else the behemoth is just sport but you might wonder if risking your life that others might depend on is a prudent course of action.<br /> <br /> But it's mostly about the other stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a DB would feel like an elemental badass and a worthy heir to the titan-slaying army of ancient myths, all the while retaining a palpable difference in raw power between the two and all the nuances this adds to their respective stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, lately when I think of the differences, I think somewhat of the idea of Dragon Blooded being less about struggling almost to the point of futility (if ever so valiant!), and more that, considering their limitations, they need a bit more set up and support and suitable environment (with an eye towards their powers having means to grant them some things). Not quite Janest fighting with incredible might if she's in a wheat field, not quite the Sidereal who keeps up arrangements that let their arcane powers actually apply to the fullest; in short, not quite the idea that a Water Aspect who fights underwater has power close to that of a Celestial. But more, if the ground is the sort that the Terrestrial can move in with good facility, and they've got a few traps prepared, and are quick and clever, they can apply themselves well. Dragon Blooded may be less powerful than many Exalts, but asymmetric warfare is a thing that exists.<br /> <br /> That feels like a closer approach to John's sentiments of &quot;Exalts defined by what they can't do&quot; then the idea that Terrestrials approach what they can't do as some noble struggle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T19:19:29-07:00","id":103066,"title":"","content":"I also like the idea that the current setting gives a Dragon-Blood a lot of his power as well, not just his Exaltation. At least in 2e, Terrestrials are given a specific ability spread in addition to their basic points, making them generally competent in many areas. Namely war. And since Dragon-Bloods work together, each of them with knowledge of combat tactics, it's an extremely effective interplay between them. Any of them can call out and begin coordinating their attacks together, and their different elemental advantages give them greater insight into any battle in which they are working together.<br /> <br /> As well, a Dynast's schooling, as said previously, gives them a general competence in many other areas. I've been in many campaigns as Celestial Exalts and everyone in the group almost universally never takes War, Socialize, Ride or Archery. Then I'll play a Dynast in the mixed group and it seems like I'm weak at first...except for the fact I'm the only one there that doesn't act like a Barbarian with no table manners, who can competently command an army, who can ride a horse, and who can actually use those big ballista weapons while besieged. A dragon-blood may not pack as big of a mystical punch, but a lot of the time, he is the most USEFUL bastard in the party. :.P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:40:46-07:00","id":103382,"title":"","content":"Yeah, part of the aesthetic of the Time of Tumult is that it pits the Scary Disruptive People -- Solars, Lunars, Abyssals, and so forth -- against The Man -- DBs and Sidereals. The latter have an extremely potent infrastructure, but are also comparatively dependent on that infrastructure, so they represent an entrenched, defensive power as opposed to the dynamic, offensive power of the Lunars and newcomers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:13:31-07:00","id":103663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=102710#post102710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Seriously, the common opinion among my group, which only follows Exalted tangentially, is that Vance is the only person in the current team they wouldn't consider bad)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not sure who's even on the team and what-else they wrote. But no-one strikes me as being &quot;bad&quot;. There's a few &quot;mehs&quot; if the people on the team are the people I think they are (but really, it's so hard to keep track of who wrote what), but no-one I'd want to see off the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-01-2014, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:14:24-07:00","id":103837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=103663#post103663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not sure who's even on the team and what-else they wrote. But no-one strikes me as being &quot;bad&quot;. There's a few &quot;mehs&quot; if the people on the team are the people I think they are (but really, it's so hard to keep track of who wrote what), but no-one I'd want to see off the project.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he's saying they think that the writers(minus Vance) are bad writers, but that they're bad <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> It's a thought that I've often seen, but I've never seen much evidence as to why they think that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:29:03-07:00","id":103845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=103020#post103020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">?__________?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry Vance. I mean, I hate to be the one to tell you this, but that guy's group is right. You don't ooze the bad-boy vibe like Holden or Hatewheel or even Eric. That's why they're swag, they get all the girls and you just get friendzoned. <br /> <br /> You could do something to make yourself seem more dangerous and compelling. Maybe take up smoking, get a leather jacket, grow a pompadour and loiter outside the local corner store.","signature":"?__________?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:34:20-07:00","id":103847,"title":"","content":"I am not sure that a group which only tangentially follows Exalted would know all the writers and be able to compare their level of badness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T01:46:29-07:00","id":103914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=103847#post103847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure that a group which only tangentially follows Exalted would know all the writers and be able to compare their level of badness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I'd like to add that I personally think that broadcasting said group's opinion, particularly when negative, is a pretty dickish thing to do :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T15:25:15-07:00","id":104376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=103847#post103847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure that a group which only tangentially follows Exalted would know all the writers and be able to compare their level of badness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, really. Perhaps they simply feel that mankind in general is inherently depraved (Vance gets a pass because they have him confused with the late Jack Vance, and assume that his continued work indicates that he's found a to transcend mortality). Or maybe the Exalted dev team abducted the group and forced them to participate in sadistic bloodsports, while Vance baked them fudge brownies and apologized for his coworker's behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:50:06-07:00","id":104484,"title":"","content":"I dunno, his handle was The Demented One for a reason...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T01:04:33-07:00","id":104686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=103845#post103845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry Vance. I mean, I hate to be the one to tell you this, but that guy's group is right. You don't ooze the bad-boy vibe like Holden or Hatewheel or even Eric. That's why they're swag, they get all the girls and you just get friendzoned.<br /> <br /> You could do something to make yourself seem more dangerous and compelling. Maybe take up smoking, get a leather jacket, grow a pompadour and loiter outside the local corner store.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Vance the George Costanza of the dev team? Ouch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T01:33:50-07:00","id":104697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102367-dragon-blooded-power-level-in-3e?p=103845#post103845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry Vance. I mean, I hate to be the one to tell you this, but that guy's group is right. You don't ooze the bad-boy vibe like Holden or Hatewheel or even Eric. That's why the